-> Spring Data JPA :
    JPA -> Jakarta Persistence API. They started giving 'specifications'. JPA doesn't have logics. It just gives set of rules and regulations.
            All ORM Framework providers follow JPA.
            JPA uses Hibernate
            Hibernate is Implementation. JPA is Specification.
            JPA is Parent, Hibernate is Child. So Hibernate has more features compared to JPA. (JPA and Spring Data JPA are not same. both are different)

    -> Spring Data JPA :    Spring Data JPA
                                   |
                                  JPA
                                   |
                                Hibernate
                                   |
                                  JDBC

